 "final_text": "All four fields submitted. Here's the grounded answer:\n\n## Did we invoice Meadow Analytics for the February executive workshop?\n\n**Yes \u2014 but not through the ERP.** Invoice **INV-2026-047** for **$18,750.00** was sent directly to Meadow Analytics on 2026-02-06.\n\n**Where it actually lives:**\n- **ERP (Dynamics/D365):** No record at all. Searched Customers, Vendors, and transaction tables exhaustively \u2014 Meadow Analytics has never been onboarded as an entity, so nothing was ever posted there.\n- **Books system:** Also empty for this counterparty (in fact the whole Books environment has zero customer/invoice records right now).\n- **Shared mailbox:** Email `em-0117` (\"Fwd: Meadow Analytics \u2014 February executive workshop invoice (sent)\", from sam.rivera@contoso-sim.example, 2026-02-06) has the actual invoice attached \u2014 bill-to Meadow Analytics, \"Executive AI workshop \u2014 February program,\" $18,750.00, Net 30, due 2026-03-08. Sam's note explains why: *\"their vendor setup in D365 is still pending with master data... Please log it in the manual tracker until the entity exists in the ERP.\"* A follow-up (`em-0118`, 2026-02-24) from Meadow's AP confirms receipt and says payment is being scheduled \u2014 but nothing confirms it was actually paid.\n- **Shared-drive tracker:** `AR-manual-invoice-log-FY26.xlsx`, row 3 \u2014 Invoice # INV-2026-047, $18,750.00, Status **\"Sent - NOT in D365\"**, note \"New client; entity setup pending with master data.\" This is exactly the off-system tracker the team uses for new clients like this one.\n- **Docs (shared drive documents):** Empty corpus \u2014 nothing found there.\n\n**Bottom line:** The paperwork is real and consistent across two independent sources (email + manual tracker), but it genuinely never made it into the ERP because Meadow Analytics' customer record doesn't exist yet. No payment or credit memo shows up anywhere, so the full **$18,750.00 is outstanding** (not yet past-due \u2014 terms are Net 30, due 2026-03-08).\n\nSubmitted: `found_in_erp: \"no\"`, `invoice_",
